\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Policy $\pi $ on one radix tree} (\eqref  {eq:action}, Alg.~\ref {alg:app}). The root is the aliased trunk $x_u$; each box is one page of $P$ tokens. Green pages are already resident on $\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {D}}$, orange pages are the miss prefilled on $\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {P}}$, and gray pages are never computed. The cascade on the right is the controller decision order: residency, protect $i{=}0$, then $(\tau _{\mathrm  {pre}},\tau _{\mathrm  {dec}})$. Only $\mathcal  {A}$ reaches $\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {P}}$ and the connector; $\mathcal  {U}$ is probed on $\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {D}}$ for $t_0$ tokens.}}{13}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:radix}{{5}{13}{\textbf {Policy $\pi $ on one radix tree} (\eqref {eq:action}, Alg.~\ref {alg:app}). The root is the aliased trunk $x_u$; each box is one page of $P$ tokens. Green pages are already resident on $\Din $, orange pages are the miss prefilled on $\Pin $, and gray pages are never computed. The cascade on the right is the controller decision order: residency, protect $i{=}0$, then $(\tau _{\mathrm {pre}},\tau _{\mathrm {dec}})$. Only $\Act $ reaches $\Pin $ and the connector; $\mathcal {U}$ is probed on $\Din $ for $t_0$ tokens}{figure.caption.30}{}}
